Question
Design PHP login module with user registration form, login form. System should use cookies to track users. Use session handling and database MySQL for login

⚙️ Installation & Setup (Using XAMPP)
1️⃣ Install XAMPP

Download and install from:
👉 https://www.apachefriends.org/

2️⃣ Start Services

Open XAMPP Control Panel and start:

Apache
MySQL

3️⃣ Project Setup
Navigate to:
C:\xampp\htdocs\
Create a project folder:
PHP_COOKIES
Copy all project files into:
htdocs/PHP_COOKIES

4️⃣ Database Setup
Open browser:
http://localhost/phpmyadmin
Create database:
user_auth
Select the database → Click Import
Import file:
schema.sql

5️⃣ Configure Database Connection

Open config.php and ensure:

$host = "localhost";
$user = "root";
$pass = "";
$db   = "user_auth";

⚠️ Make sure database name matches (user_auth)

6️⃣ Run the Project

Open in browser:

http://localhost/PHP_COOKIES/register.php


🧠 How the System Works

🔹 Registration
User enters username, email, password
Input is validated
Password is securely hashed using password_hash()
Data is stored in MySQL database

🔹 Login
User enters credentials
Password verified using password_verify()
Session is created ($_SESSION)
Optional cookie stores username ("Remember Me")

🔹 Session Handling
Session stores:
User ID
Username
Maintains login state across pages
Prevents unauthorized access

🔹 Cookie Handling
Cookie stores username
Used for auto-filling login form
Expires after 30 days

🔹 Dashboard
Accessible only after login
Checks session before granting access
Redirects unauthorized users to login page

🔹 Logout
Clears all session data
Destroys session
Deletes cookie
Redirects user to login page

🔐 Security Measures
Password hashing (password_hash)
Password verification (password_verify)
Prepared statements (prevents SQL Injection)
Session ID regeneration (prevents session fixation)
XSS protection using htmlspecialchars()
Secure cookie flags (httponly)